Author: dowiyogo <dowiyogo@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 12 09:54:36 2026 +0200

    feat(optics): port EXEC_23 explicit air-gap + Mylar reflector geometry to EndTop
    
    Ports the air-gap panel geometry from ej200_endonly/exec23-explicit-airgap
    to the EndTop build (feat/endtop-sslg4).
    
    Physics model:
    - 3 lateral face panels (−Y, +Z, −Z); ±X excluded (END SiPMs), +Y excluded
      (TOP SiPMs are barLV daughters flush with the +Y face — photons missing
      SiPMs escape through bar-air boundary and are reflected by the −Y/±Z panels)
    - Each panel: 0.10 mm air gap + 0.05 mm Mylar layer in worldLV
    - Bar→Air boundary: CreateBarSurface() dielectric_dielectric polished → TIR for
      θ > arcsin(1/1.58) = 39.3° (automatic Fresnel), no artificial REFLECTIVITY
    - Air→Mylar boundary: CreateMylarReflector() dielectric_metal R=0.95 →
      models Mylar/ESR substrate reflectance for non-TIR photons
    
    New functions added:
    - Materials::CreateMylarReflector() — AirGap→Mylar surface (dielectric_metal)
    - Materials::CreateMylar() now includes ABSLENGTH=1µm (opaque bulk)
    
    New member:
    - DetectorConstruction::fScintillatorAirSurfaces (bar↔air border surfaces)
    
    Root cause context: EXEC_23 showed that adding explicit air gap in EndOnly
    raised <Npe>_END from 0.76 → 2035 PE. The BarSkin (surface-only) approach
    in exec22 was an interim fix; this is the full geometry fix.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

